                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "same. do we need this for cgroups?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-kernel/linux/cgroup/cgroup.cfg",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "James Athappilly",
                        "email": "jamesatha@meta.com",
                        "username": "jamesatha"
                    },
                    "message": "This was needed for CONFIG_DEBUG_CGROUP_REF"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-kernel/linux/cgroup/cgroup.cfg",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-kernel/linux/cgroup/cgroup.cfg",
                    "line": 29,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "we could either leave all NET stuff off, or at least move it to another .cfg. I am not sure if everyone would want to care about net throttling individual services."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-kernel/linux/cgroup/cgroup.cfg",
                    "line": 29,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "James Athappilly",
                        "email": "jamesatha@meta.com",
                        "username": "jamesatha"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm inclined to pull out the nefilter configs into another file when we have a usec ase that would want to split it out. Right now, with our 1 use case where we want all of this, I feel like creating more distro overrides isn't the way to go"
                },
